{"SurveyID":"SV_eQbYkLxGIFmBefQ","Element":"SQ","PrimaryAttribute":"QID10","SecondaryAttribute":"Careful: Attention Check\u00a0 In some versions of the study, we included a scenario that tests if you..","TertiaryAttribute":null,"Payload":{"QuestionText":"<div style=\"text-align: center;\"><b>Careful: Attention Check&nbsp;<\/b><\/div>\n\n<div style=\"text-align: left;\"><br>\nIn some versions of the study, we included a scenario that tests if you are actually reading the scenarios or not. If the answer indicated that you did not read the scenario, <strong>the survey will stop and you will not be paid<\/strong>. If you continue, we assume that you are fine with this procedure. Otherwise, please stop now.&nbsp;<\/div>","DefaultChoices":false,"QuestionType":"DB","Selector":"TB","DataVisibility":{"Private":false,"Hidden":false},"Configuration":{"QuestionDescriptionOption":"UseText"},"QuestionDescription":"Careful: Attention Check\u00a0 In some versions of the study, we included a scenario that tests if you...","ChoiceOrder":[],"Validation":{"Settings":{"Type":"None"}},"GradingData":[],"Language":[],"NextChoiceId":7,"NextAnswerId":1,"QuestionText_Unsafe":"<div style=\"text-align: center;\"><b>Careful: Attention Check&nbsp;<\/b><\/div>\n\n<div style=\"text-align: left;\"><br>\nIn some versions of the study, we included a scenario that tests if you are actually reading the scenarios or not. If the answer indicated that you did not read the scenario, <strong>the survey will stop and you will not be paid<\/strong>. If you continue, we assume that you are fine with this procedure. Otherwise, please stop now.&nbsp;<\/div>","DataExportTag":"Q1","QuestionID":"QID10"}},
{"SurveyID":"SV_eQbYkLxGIFmBefQ","Element":"SQ","PrimaryAttribute":"QID733","SecondaryAttribute":"Collapsing Buildings After an earthquake in Lusmeara, two buildings which each contain interconne...","TertiaryAttribute":null,"Payload":{"QuestionText":"<b>Collapsing Buildings<\/b><br><br>\n\n\nAfter an earthquake in Lusmeara, two buildings which each contain interconnecting towers are at the verge of collapse. Due to the stressful circumstances, the workforce is spread thin and only one of the two buildings can be sent aid. \n<br>\nThe rescue team has to make a decision between two choices:\n<br><br>\n\n<ul>\n\n<li>\n<i>Option1<\/i>:\nSend aid to the north building, evacuating one tower while blockading the other to reduce the risk of building collapse. This would kill 300 people in the blockaded tower, while saving 400 people in the evacuated tower.\n\n<\/li>\n\n<li>\n<i>Option2<\/i>:\nSend aid to the south building, evacuating one tower while blockading the other to reduce the risk of building collapse. This would kill 3000 people in the blockaded tower, while saving 4000 people in the evacuated tower\n\n<\/li>\n\n<\/ul><br>\n\n\nIf the rescue team decided to send aid to the north building, ...<br>","DefaultChoices":false,"DataExportTag":"Q732","QuestionType":"TE","Selector":"FORM","Configuration":{"QuestionDescriptionOption":"UseText"},"QuestionDescription":"Collapsing Buildings After an earthquake in Lusmeara, two buildings which each contain interconne...","Validation":{"Settings":{"ForceResponse":"OFF"}},"GradingData":[],"Language":[],"NextChoiceId":3,"NextAnswerId":1,"SearchSource":{"AllowFreeResponse":"false"},"QuestionID":"QID733","Choices":{"1":{"Display":"How many lives will be saved?","TextEntry":"on","TextEntryValidation":"ValidNumber"},"2":{"Display":"How many lives will be sacrificed?","TextEntry":"on","TextEntryValidation":"ValidNumber"}},"ChoiceOrder":[1,2],"DataVisibility":{"Private":false,"Hidden":false}}},
{"SurveyID":"SV_eQbYkLxGIFmBefQ","Element":"SQ","PrimaryAttribute":"QID2","SecondaryAttribute":"Consent Form\u00a0 We would like to invite you to take part in a research study.\u00a0Before you decide whe.","TertiaryAttribute":null,"Payload":{"QuestionText":"<div style=\"text-align: center;\"><span style=\"font-size:16px;\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial,Helvetica,sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-weight: bolder;\">Consent Form&nbsp;<\/span><\/span><\/span><\/div>\n\n<div><span style=\"font-size:16px;\"><span style=\"font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif;\">We would like to invite you to take part in a research study.&nbsp;Before you decide whether you would like to take part it is important that you understand why the research is being done and what it would involve.&nbsp;<\/span><span style=\"font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif; text-align: center;\">Please take time to carefully read the following <\/span><a href=\"https:\/\/cityunilondon.eu.qualtrics.com\/CP\/File.php?F=F_bPCi9f3sr6MzOWV\" target=\"_blank\">Participant Information Sheet<\/a> <span style=\"font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif; text-align: center;\">(click on link).&nbsp;<\/span><span style=\"font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif;\">Please then tick the boxes below to indicate that you have read and understood the information provided in the information sheet.<\/span><\/span><\/div>","DefaultChoices":false,"QuestionType":"Matrix","Selector":"Likert","SubSelector":"SingleAnswer","DataVisibility":{"Private":false,"Hidden":false},"Configuration":{"QuestionDescriptionOption":"UseText","TextPosition":"inline","ChoiceColumnWidthPixels":557,"RepeatHeaders":"none","WhiteSpace":"OFF","MobileFirst":true},"QuestionDescription":"Consent Form\u00a0 We would like to invite you to take part in a research study.\u00a0Before you decide whe...","Choices":{"1":{"Display":"<span style=\"font-family:Arial,Helvetica,sans-serif;\">I agree to take part in this City, University of London research project. I have read the participant information sheet, which I may keep for my records.<\/span>"},"2":{"Display":"<span style=\"font-family:Arial,Helvetica,sans-serif;\"><strong>I understand this will involve: Making decisions about whether or not to sacrifice the lives of a few people to save the lives of many people.<\/strong><\/span>"},"3":{"Display":"<span style=\"font-family:Arial,Helvetica,sans-serif;\">This information will be held by City as data controller and processed for the production of scientific reports<\/span>"},"4":{"Display":"<span style=\"font-family:Arial,Helvetica,sans-serif;\">The legal basis for processing your personal data will be that this research is a task in the public interest, that is City, University of London considers the lawful basis for processing personal data to fall under Article 6(1)(e) of GDPR (public task) as the processing of research participant data is necessary for learning and teaching purposes and all research with human participants by staff and students has to be scrutinised and approved by one of City&rsquo;s Research Ethics Committees.<\/span>"},"5":{"Display":"<span style=\"font-family:Arial,Helvetica,sans-serif;\">I understand that any information I provide is confidential, and that no information that could lead to the identification of any individual will be disclosed in any reports on the project, or to any other party. No identifiable personal data will be published. The identifiable data will not be shared with any other organisation.<\/span>"},"6":{"Display":"<span style=\"font-family:Arial,Helvetica,sans-serif;\">I understand that my participation is voluntary, that I can choose not to participate in part or all of the project, and that I can withdraw at any stage of the project without being penalized or disadvantaged in any way.<\/span>"},"7":{"Display":"<span style=\"font-family:Arial,Helvetica,sans-serif;\">I agree to City, University of London recording and processing this information about me. I understand that this information will be used only for the purpose(s) set out in this statement and my consent is conditional on City complying with its duties and obligations under the General Data Protection Regulation (GDPR).<\/span>"},"8":{"Display":"<span style=\"font-family:Arial,Helvetica,sans-serif;\">I agree to take part in the above study.<\/span>"}},"ChoiceOrder":[1,2,3,4,5,6,7,8],"Validation":{"Settings":{"ForceResponse":"ON","ForceResponseType":"ON","Type":"None"}},"GradingData":[],"Language":[],"NextChoiceId":9,"NextAnswerId":2,"Answers":{"1":{"Display":"Yes"}},"AnswerOrder":["1"],"ChoiceDataExportTags":false,"QuestionText_Unsafe":"<div style=\"text-align: center;\"><span style=\"font-size:16px;\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial,Helvetica,sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-weight: bolder;\">Consent Form&nbsp;<\/span><\/span><\/span><\/div>\n\n<div><span style=\"font-size:16px;\"><span style=\"font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif;\">We would like to invite you to take part in a research study.&nbsp;Before you decide whether you would like to take part it is important that you understand why the research is being done and what it would involve.&nbsp;<\/span><span style=\"font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif; text-align: center;\">Please take time to carefully read the following <\/span><a href=\"https:\/\/cityunilondon.eu.qualtrics.com\/CP\/File.php?F=F_bPCi9f3sr6MzOWV\" target=\"_blank\">Participant Information Sheet<\/a> <span style=\"font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif; text-align: center;\">(click on link).&nbsp;<\/span><span style=\"font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif;\">Please then tick the boxes below to indicate that you have read and understood the information provided in the information sheet.<\/span><\/span><\/div>","DataExportTag":"Q1","QuestionID":"QID2"}},
{"SurveyID":"SV_eQbYkLxGIFmBefQ","Element":"SQ","PrimaryAttribute":"QID8","SecondaryAttribute":"Decision Making Task \u00a0 You will now read through 12 scenarios. At the end of each paragraph, an a..","TertiaryAttribute":null,"Payload":{"QuestionText":"<p style=\"text-align: center;\"><strong>Decision Making Task<\/strong><\/p>\n\n<p style=\"text-align: center;\">&nbsp;<\/p>\n\n<p>You will now read through 12 scenarios. At the end of each paragraph, an action will be described. Your task is to indicate to what extent it is acceptable to perform the described action. At this point you must indicate on a 6-point scale whether the action is acceptable or not.&nbsp;<\/p>\n\n<p>&nbsp;<\/p>\n\n<p>\"1\" means that the action is <em>completely unacceptable<\/em> while \"6\" means that it is <em>completely acceptable<\/em>.<o:p><\/o:p><\/p>","DefaultChoices":false,"QuestionType":"DB","Selector":"TB","Configuration":{"QuestionDescriptionOption":"UseText"},"QuestionDescription":"Decision Making Task \u00a0 You will now read through 12 scenarios. At the end of each paragraph, an a...","ChoiceOrder":[],"Validation":{"Settings":{"Type":"None"}},"GradingData":[],"Language":[],"NextChoiceId":4,"NextAnswerId":1,"DataVisibility":{"Private":false,"Hidden":false},"QuestionText_Unsafe":"<p style=\"text-align: center;\"><strong>Decision Making Task<\/strong><\/p>\n\n<p style=\"text-align: center;\">&nbsp;<\/p>\n\n<p>You will now read through 12 scenarios. At the end of each paragraph, an action will be described. Your task is to indicate to what extent it is acceptable to perform the described action. At this point you must indicate on a 6-point scale whether the action is acceptable or not.&nbsp;<\/p>\n\n<p>&nbsp;<\/p>\n\n<p>\"1\" means that the action is <em>completely unacceptable<\/em> while \"6\" means that it is <em>completely acceptable<\/em>.<o:p><\/o:p><\/p>","DataExportTag":"Q1","QuestionID":"QID8"}},
