{"SurveyID":"SV_eQbYkLxGIFmBefQ","Element":"SQ","PrimaryAttribute":"QID577","SecondaryAttribute":"Fuming Hospital In a hospital complex with buildings of different sizes, there are deadly corrosi...","TertiaryAttribute":null,"Payload":{"QuestionText":"<b>Fuming Hospital<\/b><br><br>\n\n\nIn a hospital complex with buildings of different sizes, there are deadly corrosive fumes rising through the central ventilation system due to an accident in one of the laboratories in the middle of the night. The corrosive chemicals were found in two separate vents heading towards the Evergreen and Clearview buildings, respectively. If nothing is done, then the Evergreen and Clearview buildings will be exposed to the corrosive fumes. These buildings house medical equipment for the hospital.<br>\nThe control engineer can redirect one of the fumes by running to a junction in the ventilation system and opening and closing specific vents, but there is not enough time to redirect both fumes. This leaves the engineer with two options:\n<br><br>\n\n<ul>\n\n<li>\n<i>Option1<\/i>:\nRedirect the fumes heading towards Clearview building to Summer Stone building. This would destroy 10 Chrono coins worth of medical equipment in Summer Stone building but save the 90 Chrono coins worth of medical equipment in the Clearview building\n\n<\/li>\n\n<li>\n<i>Option2<\/i>:\nRedirect the fumes heading towards the Evergreen building to the Harmony Grove Building. This would destroy 20 Chrono coins worth of medical equipment in the Harmony Grove building but save the 800 Chrono coins worth of medical equipment in the Evergreen building\n\n<\/li>\n\n<\/ul><br<br><br>\n\n\nIf you were faced with this choice, would you choose option 1 or option 2?\n<br><br>\n\n","DataExportTag":"scenario.fumingHospital.econ.comparisonType.ratio_vs_victims.n_saved1.800.n_saved2.90.n_total1.820.n_total2.100.n_victims1.20.n_victims2.10.high_ratio_second","QuestionID":"QID577","QuestionType":"MC","Selector":"SAHR","SubSelector":