hrough the central ventilation system due to an accident in one of the laboratories in the middle of the night. The corrosive chemicals were found travelling towards the Evergreen building. If nothing is done, then all the patients in the Evergreen building will be killed from the exposure to the fumes. <br>\nAn on-site control engineer can redirect the fumes by running to a junction in the ventilation system and opening and closing specific vents within the ventilation system.\n<br><br>\n\n\nIf the engineer has a friend in the Evergreen building, would it be morally acceptable to redirect the fumes from the Evergreen building to the Clearview building? This would kill the 90 patients in the Clearview building but save the 60 patients in the Evergreen building.\n\n\n","QuestionID":"QID591"}},
