{"SurveyID":"SV_eQbYkLxGIFmBefQ","Element":"SQ","PrimaryAttribute":"QID159","SecondaryAttribute":"Hopsital Power Outage During a city-wide power outage, the local hospital needs to rely on backup...","TertiaryAttribute":null,"Payload":{"QuestionText":"<b>Hopsital Power Outage<\/b><br><br>\n\n\nDuring a city-wide power outage, the local hospital needs to rely on backup generators to keep laboratories running. The laboratories require electricity to cool down pathology samples. The only electrical engineer on site receives a warning that the generators for the Spring Forest building and the East Valley building are overheating and will lose power in the next 5 minutes. The engineer has just enough time to run to a switching station to replace the failing generators with power destined to other buildings. This leaves the engineer with two options\n<br><br>\n\n<ul>\n\n<li>\n<i>Option1<\/i>:\nUse the generator for the Highland building to keep the Spring Forest building powered. This will destroy 20 pathology samples in the Highland building but save 40 pathology samples in the Spring Forest building\n\n<\/li>\n\n<li>\n<i>Option2<\/i>:\nUse the generator for the Hopedale building to keep the East Valley building powered. This will destroy 10 pathology samples in the Hopedale building but save 12 pathology samples in the East Valley building.\n\n<\/li>\n\n<\/ul><br<br><br>\n\n\nIf you were faced with this choice, would you choose option 1 or option 2?\n<br><br>\n\n","DataExportTag":"scenario.powerHospital.econ.comparisonType.ratio_vs_victims.n_saved1.40.n_saved2.12.n_total1.60.n_total2.22.n_victims1.20.n_victims2.10.high_ratio_first","QuestionID":"QID159","QuestionType":"MC","Selector":"SAHR","SubSelector":"TX","QuestionDescription":"Hopsital Power Outage During a city-wide power outage, the local hospital needs to rely on backup...","Choices":{"1":{"Display":"1: Definitely Option 1"},"2":{"Display":"2"},"3":{"Display":"3"},"4":{"Display":"4"},"5":{"Display":"5"},"6":{"Di