ypically burns one village to the ground and kills all its residents, but if enough volunteers are sacrificed in the capital, the village is spared.\nThis year, the Whotnir have been chosen to provide the sacrifice. However, a group of villagers flee to hide in the capital and would survive if they make it to the capital. Their movements have been detected by the intelligence services and a commando is sent to detain them and to use them as volunteers to be sacrificed.\n<br><br>\n\n\nIf an intelligence officer has a friend with the escapees, would it be morally acceptable to misdirect the commando to an incorrect location? This would give the 200 escapees time to escape and to survive, but lead to the death of the 1000 remaining Whotnir, whose village will be set on fire.\n\n\n","QuestionID":"QID730"}},
