iagnosed as having Hyena's Ears. Giving Abacavelam to healthy people kills them. The local health department needs to decide how to deal with an outbreak of Hyena's Ears. If they decide to administer Abacavelam, they will save 20 Hyena's Ears patients, but will kill 60 healthy, misdiagnosed patients. If they do nothing, the 20 Hyena's Ears patients will die, but the 60 misdiagnosed patients will survive.\n<br><br>\n\n\nIf the head of the health department has a friend at the hospital who does not have Hyena's Ears, is it morally acceptable to administer a placebo drug, which will kill 60 Hyena's Ears patients, but save 20 misdiagnosed patients?\n\n\n","QuestionID":"QID599"}},
